      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:80:5",
      "text": [
        " ذَكَرْنَا عِنْدَهُ الزَّيْتُونَ فَقَالَ الرَّجُلُ يَجْلِبُ الرِّيَاحَ فَقَالَ لَا بَلْ يَطْرُدُ الرِّيَاحَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Mansour Bin Al Abbas, from Ibrahim Bin Muhammad al Zara’a Al Basry, from a man, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘We mentioned the Olives in his<sup>asws</sup> presence, so the man said, ‘It brings the wind’. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘No, but it dispels the wind’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Mansur ibn al-‘Abbas has narrated from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Zari‘ al-Basriy from a man who has said the following: “We mentioned olives before abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, and a man said it stirs up gas. He (the Imam) said, ‘No, it dispels gas.’” "
        ]
      }
